-- allium: 3
use "../core/score-contract.allium" as core
-- interaction-capture.allium
--
-- Browser extension that records a user's interaction with the open
-- web page and writes it down as a PiX interaction score
-- (a 3- or 5-layer "partitura" of User / Dialogue / System / ...).
--
-- The unified library that hosts both authored scores and recordings
-- is the @pix/editor library at packages/editor (canonical store: the
-- editor's IndexedDB). The walkthrough viewer that surfaces the
-- screenshot trace of a recording is specified separately in
-- packages/editor/walkthrough-viewer.allium.
--
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Ownership
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- packages/core/score-contract.allium is the canonical owner of the
-- shared data model: Score, Movement, ScoreStep, ScreenshotTrace,
-- RecordingSession, TraceSnapshot and TraceAnnotation. This spec
-- references them as external entities carrying only the fields the
-- recorder actually touches. It does not redefine them, and where the
-- two documents could disagree, core wins.
--
-- What this spec owns is the recorder: the Recorder state machine, the
-- criteria by which a DOM event becomes a captured moment, the
-- vocabulary written into the captured_* fields, and the seeding of
-- cells at capture time.
--
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Scope
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Included:
--   - Recording lifecycle: start, stop, pause, resume. Starting a
--     recording opens a RecordingSession, which appends a new Movement
--     to the score and appends snapshots to the score's one trace.
--   - Re-recording an existing score: an APPEND, never a replace. A
--     second sitting adds a second session and a second movement.
--     Nothing already captured is discarded or rewritten.
--   - Capture granularity: one ScoreStep + one TraceSnapshot per
--     accepted interaction event. Triggers vary by element kind:
--     click for buttons/links, blur-with-change for text inputs,
--     change for dropdown/checkbox/radio/file, plus drag-drop and
--     media playback. Captures are atomic; merging consecutive steps
--     is an editing affordance, not a capture-time decision.
--   - Screenshot of the visible viewport plus a normalised focus
--     region that highlights the targeted element. The region is
--     captured as observed and is never re-croppable.
--   - Mapping captured action -> PiX score column with one cell per
--     visible layer, seeded with a pixogram inferred from the
--     element kind and a verb chosen by the interaction trigger.
--   - Seeding the user layer, but only on high-confidence signals
--     (landing on a confirmation page after a submit). Otherwise the
--     layer is left empty for a person to fill.
--   - Section divisions: when a captured step lands on a different
--     "screen" (URL, document title, or browser tab) than the
--     previous step, the new step's step_title is seeded with the
--     screen's name so the editor renders a section divider.
--   - SPA screen changes: a significant DOM mutation with no change
--     of URL, title or tab is also a section boundary. The resulting
--     sections are enumerated beneath the last real section name
--     ("Carro: Paso 1", "Carro: Paso 2", ...).
--   - System events as steps: visible error UI (alert dialogs,
--     role="alert", aria-live="assertive", validation messages)
--     creates its own step in the system layer, anchored to the
--     URL where the error appeared.
--   - Hover-revealed content as annotations: when the user dwells
--     long enough on an element that reveals a tooltip / popover,
--     the revealed text is appended to the most recent step's note.
--   - Media playback: all media events are captured (play, pause,
--     seek, end), but they do not each produce a step. The first
--     play creates the step; later events on the same element attach
--     to it.
--   - Multi-site continuity: top-level navigations (including
--     cross-origin hops to a payment gateway and back) do not
--     interrupt recording. The TraceSnapshot that lands on a new
--     host is tagged boundary = crossing.
--   - Multi-tab continuity: clicks in any tab opened from a recorded
--     page (target=_blank, window.open, ctrl-click) continue to
--     append to the same active recording. Each snapshot records
--     its tab identity so the walkthrough viewer can surface
--     parallel flows. The partitura stays linear.
--   - Forensic posture: capture-derived data lives in a separate
--     ScreenshotTrace entity per Score; once written, snapshots are
--     append-only. Per-Score provenance metadata at create time.
--   - Local-only library (browser storage), survives browser restart.
--     The canonical store is the editor's IndexedDB; recordings are
--     flushed there on UserStopsRecording.
--   - Score state {draft | final}: recordings start as draft and
--     stay draft until the user explicitly promotes them.
--   - Export to two formats: PiX-JSON (round-trip with editor) and
--     a step-by-step tutorial PDF (driven by the ScreenshotTrace).
--
-- Excluded:
--   - The shared data model itself. Score, Movement, ScoreStep,
--     ScreenshotTrace, RecordingSession, TraceSnapshot and
--     TraceAnnotation belong to packages/core/score-contract.allium.
--   - Library capacity as a count. The library is bounded by storage
--     pressure, warns, and offers a backup; it never refuses a save
--     and never evicts. That policy lives in core; this spec only
--     honours it by never gating recording on library size.
--   - Free-form remarks. TraceAnnotation exists and is mutable, but
--     the recorder never writes one — the viewer does.
--   - All pictos.cl integration: aid-availability checks, in-page aid
--     overlay, sidepanel iframe to app.pictos.cl, "send task" upload,
--     and pictogram fetching from api.pictos.cl. This branch is offline.
--   - Browser-extension plumbing details (manifest shape, message bus,
--     service-worker lifetime). The browser is modelled as an external
--     boundary; specifics live in implementation, not in this spec.
--   - The PiX editor application itself. Rendering, editing
--     affordances and export live there. The walkthrough viewer for
--     the screenshot trace is specified in
--     packages/editor/walkthrough-viewer.allium.
--   - Storage backend choice. The spec only commits to "local to the
--     browser profile, persistent across sessions, never on the network".
--   - Tamper-evidence beyond append-only semantics: no hash chains, no
--     digital signatures, no trusted timestamping.
--   - Audit log of exports: exporting a Score does not mutate it.
--   - Capture of typed input values verbatim: the dialogue cell
--     describes what the user did (Escribir en email), not what they
--     typed. Password fields never reveal anything beyond the fact
--     of typing. Dropdown / checkbox / radio selections do reveal
--     the chosen option label (it is meta-data, not free text).
--   - CSS-only hover reveals. A site that shows content on hover
--     without touching the DOM is invisible to the recorder. Still
--     deferred; see Open Questions.
--
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Library locus and storage
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The editor's IndexedDB is the canonical home for both authored scores
-- and recordings. The extension does not maintain a long-term score
-- library of its own; it owns the active recording session and flushes
-- its product to the editor library on UserStopsRecording.
--
-- Authored scores are created by the editor and start at state = final.
-- Recordings are created by the extension and start at state = draft.
-- A Score's state changes only via UserMarksScoreAsFinal /
-- UserReopensScoreAsDraft.
--
-- Each recorded Score owns a ScreenshotTrace 1:1, holding the
-- screenshots and focus regions that were captured. The Score itself is
-- purely the partitura — text and pixogram cells — so it can be edited
-- without ever touching the trace. The trace is one per score and grows
-- across sittings; it is never replaced.

-- ============================================================
-- Given
-- ============================================================

-- There is one recorder per browser profile. Every rule below speaks
-- about that one instance.
given {
    recorder: Recorder
}

-- ============================================================
-- External Entities
-- ============================================================

-- The web page the user is interacting with. The extension observes
-- it; it does not own its lifecycle.
external entity WebPage {
    url: String
    title: String                           -- document.title at observation time
    viewport_width: Integer
    viewport_height: Integer

    -- Opaque browser tab identifier. Implementation: chrome.tabs.Tab.id
    -- or equivalent. The spec requires only uniqueness within the
    -- session and stability across the life of one tab.
    tab_id: String
}

-- A DOM element on the current page that the recorder considers
-- worth capturing. "Worth capturing" is defined by the
-- ElementInteractivityCriteria invariant.
external entity InteractiveElement {
    page: WebPage
    tag_name: String                        -- button | a | input | select | textarea | ...
    role: String?                           -- ARIA role, if any
    text_content: String?                   -- visible text inside the element
    aria_label: String?
    placeholder: String?                    -- for inputs
    selected_option_text: String?           -- for <select> with a current selection
    is_contenteditable: Boolean
    bounding_box: BoundingBox               -- position and size within the viewport
}

-- A media element (HTML <video> or <audio>) the user interacts with.
external entity MediaElement {
    page: WebPage
    tag_name: String                        -- "video" or "audio"
    src: String
    label: String?                          -- title attribute, aria-label, or filename
    bounding_box: BoundingBox
}

-- A visible error indicator on a page — a validation message, alert
-- dialog, role="alert" notification or similar. Detection criteria
-- live in invariant ErrorDetectionCriteria.
external entity ErrorIndicator {
    page: WebPage
    text: String                            -- the visible error message
    severity: ErrorSeverity
    role_or_aria: String?                   -- e.g., 'role=alert', 'aria-live=assertive'
    bounding_box: BoundingBox?
}

-- ------------------------------------------------------------
-- The shared score model
-- ------------------------------------------------------------
-- Owner: packages/core/score-contract.allium. Everything below is a
-- narrow view of what core defines, listing only the fields the
-- recorder reads or writes. Consult core for the full definitions,
-- the lifecycle and the cross-entity invariants.

-- Owner: packages/core/score-contract.allium.
external entity Score {
    id: String
    title: String
    description: String
    layout: ScoreLayout
    state: ScoreState
    movements: List<Movement> with score = this
    trace: ScreenshotTrace?                 -- absent until the first sitting
    created_at: Timestamp
    updated_at: Timestamp

    -- Provenance is written once, by the recorder, at Score creation.
    -- It is not part of core's Score today; see Open Questions.
    provenance: ScoreProvenance

    visible_layers:
        if layout = pix:
            { user, dialogue, system }
        else:
            { environment, user, dialogue, system, supporting_processes }
}

-- Owner: packages/core/score-contract.allium.
--
-- A movement is a recording session's worth of steps. That is the
-- meaning the recorder gives it and the reason a second sitting
-- appends one rather than reopening the last.
external entity Movement {
    id: String
    score: Score
    position: Integer                       -- 0-based index within score.movements
    steps: List<ScoreStep> with movement = this
}

-- Owner: packages/core/score-contract.allium.
--
-- One column of the PiX grid — partitura content only. Capture-derived
-- data lives in the matching TraceSnapshot. The five cell fields are
-- named for their layers, matching the serialised field names; a step
-- carries all five whatever the layout.
external entity ScoreStep {
    id: String
    movement: Movement
    position: Integer                       -- 0-based index within movement.steps
    step_title: String                      -- non-empty marks the start of a section
    note: String                            -- caption below the grid; can include
                                            -- hover-reveal annotations, media events
                                            -- and error context

    environment: Cell
    user: Cell
    dialogue: Cell
    system: Cell
    supporting_processes: Cell

    snapshot: TraceSnapshot?                -- the evidence behind this step, when the
                                            -- step was recorded rather than typed
}

-- Owner: packages/core/score-contract.allium.
--
-- One trace per recorded Score. It grows across sittings; a second
-- recording appends to it and never replaces it.
external entity ScreenshotTrace {
    id: String
    score: Score
    snapshots: List<TraceSnapshot> with trace = this
    sessions: List<RecordingSession> with trace = this
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- Owner: packages/core/score-contract.allium.
--
-- One sitting at the recorder. The recorder opens one on start and
-- closes it on stop. At most one is live at a time.
external entity RecordingSession {
    id: String
    trace: ScreenshotTrace
    movement: Movement                      -- the movement this session appended
    index: Integer                          -- 0-based, in order of recording
    started_at: Timestamp
    ended_at: Timestamp?                    -- absent while the session is live

    is_live: not exists ended_at
}

-- Owner: packages/core/score-contract.allium.
--
-- The empirical record of one captured interaction.
--
-- Core types the captured_* fields and boundary as opaque strings,
-- deliberately: interpreting them is the recorder's business, not the
-- contract's. This spec supplies that interpretation, so it types them
-- with the enums it writes. Likewise, core makes them optional because
-- a snapshot extracted from a legacy score may lack them; every
-- snapshot written by the rules below carries all of them, which is why
-- they are not optional in this view.
external entity TraceSnapshot {
    id: String
    trace: ScreenshotTrace
    session: RecordingSession               -- which sitting produced it
    step: ScoreStep                         -- referenced by step.id

    screenshot: String                      -- data URL of the viewport
    focus: FocusRegion
    captured_at: Timestamp
    captured_from_url: String
    captured_page_title: String
    captured_tab_id: String
    captured_kind: CapturedElementKind
    captured_trigger: InteractionTrigger
    boundary: BoundaryMarker
}

-- Owner: packages/core/score-contract.allium.
--
-- A free-form remark someone attaches to a captured moment after the
-- fact. Declared here only so it is visible that the recorder does not
-- write one: annotations are commentary, added in the viewer, and
-- their existence is why a snapshot never needs editing.
external entity TraceAnnotation {
    id: String
    snapshot: TraceSnapshot
    text: String
}

-- A serialized PiX score, conforming to the data contract owned by
-- @pix/core. Designed to open directly in the PiX web editor.
-- Screenshots and other capture-derived data are NOT part of the
-- score document — they live in the ScreenshotTrace.
external entity PiXScoreDocument {
    score_id: String                        -- target Score.id
    payload: String                         -- the JSON document (no screenshots)
}

-- A step-by-step tutorial PDF generated from a Score's ScreenshotTrace.
external entity TutorialPdf {
    score_id: String
    payload: String                         -- the encoded document
}

-- ============================================================
-- Value Types
-- ============================================================

value BoundingBox {
    x: Integer                              -- pixels from viewport left
    y: Integer                              -- pixels from viewport top
    width: Integer
    height: Integer
}

-- One (layer x step) cell. Owner of the shape: score-contract.allium.
--
-- A cell is a single encoded string, not a pair. It may carry a
-- pixogram alone, text alone, or both, and the encoding expresses all
-- three without a special case. The pixogram name and the text are
-- derived from that string, never stored beside it.
value Cell {
    raw: String                             -- "" for an empty cell

    icon: parse_pixogram_name(raw)          -- catalogue name, or null when the
                                            -- leading token is not one
    text: parse_cell_text(raw)              -- the remainder, trimmed
    is_empty: raw = ""
}

-- The highlighted region drawn over the screenshot in the viewer.
-- Stored as percentages of the screenshot dimensions so the highlight
-- survives image resizing.
value FocusRegion {
    x_percent: Decimal                      -- 0..100, centre x as % of width
    y_percent: Decimal                      -- 0..100, centre y as % of height
    radius_percent: Decimal                 -- 0..100, as % of half the longest edge
}

-- Provenance metadata captured once at Score creation.
value ScoreProvenance {
    user_agent: String
    extension_version: String
    timezone: String                        -- IANA name, e.g. "America/Santiago"
    locale: String                          -- BCP-47 tag, e.g. "es-CL"
}

-- ============================================================
-- Enumerations
-- ============================================================

-- The five PiX layers. `supporting_processes` is the name of the
-- layer, everywhere; the short alias `supporting` is retired.
enum ScoreLayer {
    user | dialogue | system | environment | supporting_processes
}

enum ScoreLayout {
    pix                                     -- 3 layers: user, dialogue, system
    | sb                                    -- 5 layers: + environment, supporting_processes
}

enum ScoreState {
    draft                                   -- needs human refinement
    | final                                 -- authored or promoted
}

-- How the recorder classified the targeted element. Drives the
-- pixogram seeded into the dialogue cell.
enum CapturedElementKind {
    button | link | text_input | password_input | checkbox | radio
    | dropdown | text_area | file_input | media | drag_source
    | drag_target | error_surface | generic
}

-- What kind of interaction triggered the capture. Drives the verb
-- chosen for the dialogue cell text. Orthogonal to CapturedElementKind:
-- the same element kind can produce different InteractionTriggers
-- (a checkbox can be triggered by `change`, but never by a bare click
-- — see invariant TriggerMatchesKind).
enum InteractionTrigger {
    click                                   -- mouse click on a clickable element
    | text_committed                        -- input/textarea blurred with value changed
    | selection_committed                   -- dropdown/checkbox/radio changed
    | file_attached                         -- <input type=file> received a file
    | drag_drop                             -- source dragged and dropped on target
    | media_play                            -- <video>/<audio> started playing
    | system_error                          -- error UI became visible (system-emitted)
}

-- Everything a media element can report. All four are captured; only
-- the first `play` on a given element creates a step.
enum MediaEventKind {
    play | paused | seeked | ended
}

enum ErrorSeverity {
    error | warning | info
}

-- Marks a TraceSnapshot that landed on a different host than the
-- previous snapshot in its trace.
enum BoundaryMarker {
    none                                    -- same host as previous, or first snapshot
    | crossing                              -- this snapshot's host differs
}

-- ============================================================
-- Entities and Variants
-- ============================================================

-- The single global recording state for the extension. There is one
-- recorder per browser profile, bound as `recorder` in the given block.
entity Recorder {
    state: idle | recording | paused
    active_score: Score?
    active_session: RecordingSession?       -- the sitting currently open
    active_tab: String?                     -- tab where the most recent capture occurred

    -- Section naming state. `last_section_base` is the name of the last
    -- real screen change (document title, or the screen's name).
    -- `spa_section_ordinal` counts the in-place screen changes observed
    -- beneath it, and is reset to 0 by every real screen change.
    last_section_base: String
    spa_section_ordinal: Integer
    pending_section_title: String           -- "" when the next capture starts no section

    transitions state {
        idle -> recording                   -- UserStartsRecording
        recording -> paused                 -- UserPausesRecording
        paused -> recording                 -- UserResumesRecording
        recording -> idle                   -- UserStopsRecording
        paused -> idle                      -- UserStopsRecording (from paused)
        terminal: idle
    }
}

-- ============================================================
-- Config
-- ============================================================

config {
    -- Pixogram names seeded into the dialogue cell, by element kind.
    -- These are catalogue names; how a name is encoded into a cell's
    -- raw string is the codec's business (see core's CellEncoding).
    icon_button: String = "button"
    icon_link: String = "link"
    icon_text_input: String = "input"
    icon_password_input: String = "password"
    icon_checkbox: String = "checkbox"
    icon_radio: String = "radioselect"
    icon_dropdown: String = "select"
    icon_text_area: String = "text"
    icon_file_input: String = "attach"
    icon_drag: String = "drag"
    icon_drop: String = "drop"
    icon_media_play: String = "play"
    icon_error: String = "alert"
    icon_generic_click: String = "click"

    -- Pixogram seeded into the system cell when the URL changed
    -- since the previous captured step.
    icon_navigation: String = "page"

    -- Pixogram seeded into the *user* cell on a high-confidence
    -- success signal. The author's example: landing on a confirmation
    -- page after a submit.
    icon_user_success: String = "happy"

    -- Fraction of the profile's storage quota at which the library is
    -- considered under pressure. Mirrors core's parameter of the same
    -- name; crossing it warns and offers a backup, and nothing else.
    library_pressure_fraction: Decimal = 0.8

    -- Coarse backstop for browsers that will not report a quota. Not
    -- the real bound — the real bound is weight. Mirrors core.
    score_count_backstop: Integer = 20

    -- Debounce window for re-scanning interactive elements after
    -- DOM mutations. Below this, mutation bursts are coalesced.
    interactive_rescan_debounce: Duration = 300.milliseconds

    -- Fraction of the rendered subtree that must change, within one
    -- debounce window and with no change of URL, title or tab, for the
    -- recorder to read it as an in-place screen change.
    spa_section_mutation_threshold: Decimal = 0.4

    -- Word used when enumerating in-place screen changes beneath the
    -- last real section name: "Carro: Paso 1", "Carro: Paso 2".
    spa_section_step_label: String = "Paso"

    -- A hover that reveals a tooltip/popover only counts as a
    -- capture-worthy "hover reveal" if the user dwells this long.
    hover_capture_threshold: Duration = 1500.milliseconds

    -- Errors observed within this window of one another are
    -- coalesced into a single SystemErrorCapturesStep firing
    -- (so a validation that surfaces 3 messages at once becomes
    -- one step, not three).
    error_coalesce_window: Duration = 500.milliseconds
}

-- ============================================================
-- Defaults
-- ============================================================

default Cell empty_cell = { raw: "" }

-- ============================================================
-- Rules — Score creation
-- ============================================================

rule UserCreatesScore {
    when: UserCreatesScore(layout, title?)

    -- No capacity gate. Storage pressure warns and offers a backup; it
    -- never refuses. Refusing here would strand work that has nowhere
    -- else to go — the library is the only copy.
    --
    -- Authored scores skip the draft phase; they have no trace and no
    -- session until someone records against them.
    ensures:
        let score = Score.created(
            id: new_id(),
            title: title ?? "",
            description: "",
            layout: layout,
            state: final,
            trace: null,
            provenance: capture_provenance(),
            created_at: now,
            updated_at: now
        )
        Movement.created(
            id: new_id(),
            score: score,
            position: 0
        )
}

-- ============================================================
-- Rules — Recording lifecycle
-- ============================================================

-- Recording against a score that has already been recorded is an
-- APPEND. A second sitting opens a second RecordingSession, which
-- appends a second Movement to the partitura and appends its snapshots
-- to the same trace. Nothing captured before is discarded or rewritten.
--
-- The trace is created here only if the score has none — that is, only
-- on the first sitting.
rule UserStartsRecording {
    when: UserStartsRecording(score)

    requires: recorder.state = idle
    requires: score.state = draft

    ensures: recorder.state = recording
    ensures: recorder.active_score = score
    ensures:
        if not exists score.trace:
            let trace = ScreenshotTrace.created(
                score: score,
                created_at: now
            )
            score.trace = trace
    ensures: RecordingSessionOpened(score: score)
}

-- Split from UserStartsRecording so the session and its movement are
-- opened against a trace that is known to exist, whether it was just
-- created or has been there since an earlier sitting.
rule OpenRecordingSession {
    when: RecordingSessionOpened(score)

    requires: exists score.trace

    ensures:
        let movement = Movement.created(
            id: new_id(),
            score: score,
            position: score.movements.count
        )
        let session = RecordingSession.created(
            id: new_id(),
            trace: score.trace,
            movement: movement,
            index: score.trace.sessions.count,
            started_at: now,
            ended_at: null
        )
        recorder.active_session = session
        recorder.last_section_base = ""
        recorder.spa_section_ordinal = 0
        recorder.pending_section_title = ""
        score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserPausesRecording {
    when: UserPausesRecording(session)

    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: recorder.active_session = session

    -- While paused, no capture event of any kind produces a step. The
    -- session stays live and active_score is preserved, so resume
    -- continues appending to the same movement — a pause is not a
    -- sitting boundary. Per @guarantee RecordingStateAlwaysVisible the
    -- overlay reflects the paused state distinctly (e.g. the dot stops
    -- pulsing).
    ensures: recorder.state = paused
}

rule UserResumesRecording {
    when: UserResumesRecording(session)

    requires: recorder.state = paused
    requires: recorder.active_session = session

    ensures: recorder.state = recording
}

rule UserStopsRecording {
    when: UserStopsRecording(session)

    requires: recorder.state = recording or recorder.state = paused
    requires: recorder.active_session = session

    let score = recorder.active_score

    -- Closing the session is what makes the sitting legible later: a
    -- comparison view sorts by session index, and without the boundary
    -- two runs of the same task would be one long run.
    ensures: session.ended_at = now

    ensures: recorder.state = idle
    ensures: recorder.active_score = null
    ensures: recorder.active_session = null
    ensures: recorder.active_tab = null

    -- The recording (Score + ScreenshotTrace) is persisted to the
    -- editor's canonical library at the moment the recorder stops.
    -- See @guarantee RecordingPersistedOnStop. The Score's state
    -- remains draft until UserMarksScoreAsFinal fires.
    ensures: RecordingFlushedToLibrary(score: score, session: session)
}

-- ============================================================
-- Rules — Capture
-- ============================================================

-- Every accepted firing produces exactly one ScoreStep + one
-- TraceSnapshot, except UserHoverRevealsContent and
-- MediaEventAttachesToStep, which annotate an existing step — see
-- invariant CaptureGranularity.
--
-- The shared structure:
--   * derive interaction kind, element kind, trigger
--   * compute dialogue text from auto_caption (per-trigger verb
--     mapping; NEVER includes typed text from <input> values; DOES
--     include selected option text from dropdown/checkbox/radio)
--   * seed the user cell only on a high-confidence signal
--   * detect section break (URL/title/tab change, or a pending SPA
--     section title left by SpaScreenChangeStartsSection)
--   * detect boundary crossing (host change)
--   * build the step + snapshot in the active session's movement

rule UserClickCapturesStep {
    when: UserClicksElement(element)

    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session
    -- Click is the trigger for elements whose primary interaction is
    -- the click itself: buttons, links, generic clickables. Inputs
    -- and selectors have their own dedicated triggers below.
    requires: classify_element(element) in
        { button, link, generic, drag_source }

    let trigger = click
    let element_kind = classify_element(element)

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            session: recorder.active_session,
            element: element,
            element_kind: element_kind,
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserTextInputCapturesStep {
    when: UserBlursTextInput(element, text_changed)

    -- Text inputs (single-line, multi-line, password, contenteditable)
    -- capture on blur, only if the value changed during the focus
    -- session. This matches the user's intent: they wrote something.
    -- A pure focus-then-blur with no change does not capture.
    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session
    requires: text_changed = true
    requires: classify_element(element) in
        { text_input, password_input, text_area }
        or element.is_contenteditable

    let trigger = text_committed

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            session: recorder.active_session,
            element: element,
            element_kind: classify_element(element),
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserSelectionCapturesStep {
    when: UserChangesSelection(element, new_value)

    -- Dropdowns (<select>, role=listbox/combobox), checkboxes (and
    -- toggle switches), radios. Capture fires on the change event,
    -- when the value flips. The new value is included verbatim in
    -- the dialogue text — for these kinds it is choice meta-data,
    -- not free user input.
    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session
    requires: classify_element(element) in
        { dropdown, checkbox, radio }

    let trigger = selection_committed

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            session: recorder.active_session,
            element: element,
            element_kind: classify_element(element),
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserFileAttachmentCapturesStep {
    when: UserAttachesFile(element, file_count, file_names)

    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session
    requires: classify_element(element) = file_input

    let trigger = file_attached

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            session: recorder.active_session,
            element: element,
            element_kind: file_input,
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserDragDropCapturesStep {
    when: UserDragsAndDrops(source, target)

    -- One drag-drop is ONE step, captured once, at the drop. The
    -- source identity survives as text in the partitura ("Arrastrar
    -- source a target"); the screenshot is the viewport at the moment
    -- of drop and the focus region is on the target.
    --
    -- No second snapshot at drag-start. Showing the source "in flight"
    -- would double the storage cost of every drag for a picture of a
    -- moment nobody reads back, and the machinery to capture it fairly
    -- (which frame? mid-flight or at pickup?) costs more than the
    -- imprecision does.
    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session

    let trigger = drag_drop

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            session: recorder.active_session,
            element: target,
            element_kind: drag_target,
            trigger: trigger,
            secondary_element: source        -- consumed by auto_caption
        )
}

-- Media: capture everything, but do not multiply steps.
--
-- The first play on an element creates the step. Every later event on
-- that same element — pause, seek, end, a second play — attaches to it.
-- A user who cares about a particular moment of playback can say so in
-- the note or in a TraceAnnotation; what they must not get is a
-- partitura with forty columns because someone scrubbed a video.

rule MediaFirstPlayCapturesStep {
    when: MediaElementEvent(media, event_kind)

    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session
    requires: event_kind = play
    requires: not exists step_for_media(recorder.active_session, media)

    let trigger = media_play

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            session: recorder.active_session,
            element: media,                  -- treated as InteractiveElement-like
            element_kind: media,
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule MediaEventAttachesToStep {
    when: MediaElementEvent(media, event_kind)

    -- Pause, seek, end and re-play all land here once the element has
    -- a step. An event on an element the recorder never saw start
    -- (playback began before recording, or on a page it could not
    -- inject into) matches neither rule and is dropped — there is no
    -- honest step to attach it to.
    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session

    let step = step_for_media(recorder.active_session, media)

    requires: exists step

    ensures: step.note = append_media_event(step.note, event_kind, now)
    ensures: step.movement.score.updated_at = now
}

rule SystemErrorCapturesStep {
    when: ErrorBecameVisible(indicator)

    -- A visible error UI on a recorded page becomes its own step.
    -- The dialogue cell shows the error text with the alert
    -- pixogram. The system cell echoes the alert (the system is
    -- speaking). The user cell stays empty here — an error is not a
    -- high-confidence signal about how the person felt, and guessing
    -- would be worse than leaving it for them.
    --
    -- Coalescing: errors that surface within
    -- config.error_coalesce_window of one another collapse into
    -- one step, with their texts joined.
    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session

    let trigger = system_error

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            session: recorder.active_session,
            element: indicator,
            element_kind: error_surface,
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserHoverRevealsContent {
    when: HoverRevealedContent(element, revealed_text, duration)

    -- A hover that reveals a tooltip / popover for at least
    -- config.hover_capture_threshold annotates the most recent
    -- step's note. It does NOT create a new step — hover is
    -- auxiliary information, not a moment of interaction.
    --
    -- If no step exists yet (the user hasn't done anything else),
    -- the hover is silently dropped (no anchor for the annotation).
    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: duration >= config.hover_capture_threshold
    requires: revealed_text != ""
    requires: exists recorder.active_session

    let movement = recorder.active_session.movement
    let last_step = latest_step(movement)

    requires: exists last_step

    ensures: last_step.note = append_hover_annotation(last_step.note, revealed_text)
    ensures: movement.score.updated_at = now
}

-- ------------------------------------------------------------
-- In-place (SPA) screen changes
-- ------------------------------------------------------------

-- An SPA wizard renders three moments of a cart in place: same URL,
-- same document.title, same tab. SectionStartsOnScreenChange cannot
-- see them, so the recorder falls back to the shape of the page:
-- a large enough DOM mutation, within one debounce window and with no
-- change of URL, title or tab, is read as a new screen.
--
-- The recorder cannot name what it cannot read, so it does not try.
-- It inherits the last real section name and enumerates beneath it:
-- "Carro", then "Carro: Paso 1", "Carro: Paso 2". The person renames
-- them afterwards; the numbering exists so the divider lands in the
-- right column, not to be the final wording.
rule SpaScreenChangeStartsSection {
    when: SignificantDomMutation(page, changed_fraction)

    requires: recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists recorder.active_session
    requires: changed_fraction >= config.spa_section_mutation_threshold
    requires: recorder.last_section_base != ""

    -- The ordinal is read pre-rule on the right-hand side, so the name
    -- and the counter both land on the same value.
    ensures: recorder.spa_section_ordinal = recorder.spa_section_ordinal + 1
    ensures: recorder.pending_section_title =
        spa_section_name(
            recorder.last_section_base,
            recorder.spa_section_ordinal + 1,
            config.spa_section_step_label
        )
}

-- ============================================================
-- Rules — Manual editing
-- ============================================================

-- Manual editor actions (no click capture involved).

rule UserAddsBlankStep {
    when: UserAddsBlankStep(movement)

    -- Manually-added steps have no matching TraceSnapshot.
    ensures:
        ScoreStep.created(
            id: new_id(),
            movement: movement,
            position: movement.steps.count,
            step_title: "",
            note: "",
            environment: empty_cell,
            user: empty_cell,
            dialogue: empty_cell,
            system: empty_cell,
            supporting_processes: empty_cell,
            snapshot: null
        )
        movement.score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserEditsCell {
    when: UserEditsCell(step, layer, new_value)

    ensures:
        if layer = user:                        step.user = new_value
        else if layer = dialogue:               step.dialogue = new_value
        else if layer = system:                 step.system = new_value
        else if layer = environment:            step.environment = new_value
        else:                                   step.supporting_processes = new_value
        step.movement.score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserEditsScoreMetadata {
    when: UserEditsScoreMetadata(score, title?, description?, layout?)

    ensures:
        if exists title:        score.title = title
        if exists description:  score.description = description
        if exists layout:       score.layout = layout
        score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserDeletesStep {
    when: UserDeletesStep(step)

    let score = step.movement.score

    -- The evidence goes with the step. A snapshot whose step is gone
    -- is orphaned and expensive: screenshots dominate the profile's
    -- quota.
    ensures:
        if exists step.snapshot:
            not exists step.snapshot
    ensures: not exists step
    ensures: score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserDeletesScore {
    when: UserDeletesScore(score)

    requires: recorder.active_score != score

    ensures:
        if exists score.trace:
            for s in score.trace.snapshots:
                not exists s
            for sess in score.trace.sessions:
                not exists sess
            not exists score.trace
    ensures: not exists score
}

rule UserDeletesTrace {
    when: UserDeletesTrace(score)

    requires: exists score.trace
    requires: recorder.active_score != score

    ensures:
        for s in score.trace.snapshots:
            not exists s
    ensures:
        for sess in score.trace.sessions:
            not exists sess
    ensures: not exists score.trace
    ensures: score.trace = null
    ensures: score.updated_at = now
}

-- ============================================================
-- Rules — Score state
-- ============================================================

rule UserMarksScoreAsFinal {
    when: UserMarksScoreAsFinal(score)

    requires: score.state = draft

    ensures: score.state = final
    ensures: score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserReopensScoreAsDraft {
    when: UserReopensScoreAsDraft(score)

    requires: score.state = final

    ensures: score.state = draft
    ensures: score.updated_at = now
}

-- ============================================================
-- Rules — Export and re-import
-- ============================================================

rule UserExportsScoreAsPiXJson {
    when: UserExportsScoreAsPiXJson(score)

    ensures:
        PiXScoreDocument.created(
            score_id: score.id,
            payload: pix_json_of(
                score: score,
                with_ids: true
            )
        )
}

rule UserExportsScoreAsPdf {
    when: UserExportsScoreAsPdf(score)

    ensures:
        TutorialPdf.created(
            score_id: score.id,
            payload: pdf_tutorial_of(
                score: score,
                trace: score.trace,
                page_per_snapshot: true
            )
        )

    -- The instruction text under each page is the dialogue cell's
    -- text, i.e. Cell.text of ScoreStep.dialogue.
}

rule UserImportsPiXScore {
    when: UserImportsPiXScore(target_score, document)

    requires: target_score.id = document.score_id

    -- The trace is NEVER touched by re-import — the document never
    -- carries snapshots. Replace-in-place applies to partitura fields
    -- only, and steps keep their ids so the trace stays joined.
    ensures: PiXDocumentReconciled(
        target: target_score,
        document: document
    )
    ensures: target_score.updated_at = now
}

-- ============================================================
-- Invariants
-- ============================================================

invariant ElementInteractivityCriteria {
    -- An InteractiveElement is one for which any of the following holds:
    --   1. tag_name in {button, a, input, select, textarea}
    --   2. ARIA role in {button, link, checkbox, radio, menuitem, tab,
    --      listbox, option, switch, searchbox, textbox, combobox}
    --   3. has an onclick attribute, or is an `a` with an href
    --   4. has tabindex other than -1
    --   5. has contenteditable = "true"
    -- Open and closed shadow roots are traversed. The set is rebuilt
    -- on DOM mutations, debounced by interactive_rescan_debounce.
}

invariant ErrorDetectionCriteria {
    -- An ErrorIndicator becomes visible when a DOM element matches
    -- ANY of:
    --   1. role = "alert" or role = "alertdialog"
    --   2. aria-live = "assertive" with non-empty text content
    --   3. element class matches a common error pattern:
    --      "alert-danger", "error", "form-error", "validation-error",
    --      "is-invalid", or similar (locale-agnostic, class-based).
    --   4. <dialog> with text containing locale-agnostic error tokens
    --      ("error", "failed", "invalid", "denied", or their
    --      translations as the implementation sees fit).
    -- The element must be visible (not display: none, not aria-hidden).
    -- Detection runs on DOM mutations, coalesced by
    -- error_coalesce_window so a burst of validation messages
    -- becomes one capture, not many.
}

invariant HoverRevealCriteria {
    -- A "hover reveal" is captured when:
    --   1. The user's cursor stays over the same element for at least
    --      hover_capture_threshold.
    --   2. During that dwell, a tooltip / popover element became
    --      visible (a new element appeared in the DOM, either from
    --      the title attribute, ARIA describedby, or any descendant
    --      with role = "tooltip" / role = "status").
    --   3. The revealed element has non-empty text content.
    -- Mouse-leave or keyboard activity before the threshold cancels
    -- the capture.
    --
    -- A reveal driven purely by CSS — no DOM change, only a computed
    -- style flipping — is invisible to this and stays uncaptured. See
    -- Open Questions.
}

invariant CaptureGranularity {
    -- Exactly one ScoreStep + one TraceSnapshot per accepted firing of
    -- one of the capture rules:
    --   - UserClickCapturesStep
    --   - UserTextInputCapturesStep
    --   - UserSelectionCapturesStep
    --   - UserFileAttachmentCapturesStep
    --   - UserDragDropCapturesStep
    --   - MediaFirstPlayCapturesStep
    --   - SystemErrorCapturesStep
    -- UserHoverRevealsContent and MediaEventAttachesToStep do NOT
    -- create a step; they annotate an existing one. Those are the two
    -- explicit exceptions to "one event, one column".
    --
    -- An "accepted" firing means the Recorder is in state = recording
    -- with a live session (paused suspends capture entirely, see
    -- PauseSuspendsCapture) and the kind/trigger combination is
    -- permitted by TriggerMatchesKind.
    --
    -- Capture is atomic and stays atomic. Consecutive captures within
    -- one form or component are never collapsed at capture time: the
    -- recorder writes what happened, and merging is an editing
    -- decision made later, in the editor, with the steps in view. A
    -- merge that turns out wrong can be undone; a capture that never
    -- happened cannot be recovered.
}

invariant TriggerMatchesKind {
    -- Each TraceSnapshot has a captured_kind and a captured_trigger.
    -- The combinations the spec permits:
    --   click           with kind in {button, link, generic, drag_source}
    --   text_committed  with kind in {text_input, password_input, text_area}
    --                   or contenteditable=true elements
    --   selection_committed with kind in {dropdown, checkbox, radio}
    --   file_attached   with kind = file_input
    --   drag_drop       with kind = drag_target (the destination)
    --   media_play      with kind = media
    --   system_error    with kind = error_surface
    -- Any other combination is a contract violation, never produced
    -- by the rules in this spec.
}

invariant PauseSuspendsCapture {
    -- While Recorder.state = paused, NO capture rule fires. Events
    -- that would otherwise trigger a capture are silently dropped.
    -- The recorder is "asleep but not dead": the session stays live,
    -- the active_score and its trace remain intact, and resuming
    -- continues to append to the same movement.
    --
    -- A pause is therefore not a sitting boundary. Only stop-then-start
    -- opens a new session and a new movement.
}

invariant ScreenshotScope {
    -- A captured screenshot is the visible viewport of the active
    -- tab at capture time, encoded as a JPEG data URL. Off-screen
    -- page content is not captured. The focus region marks the
    -- targeted element's bounding box at capture time, normalised
    -- to percentages so the overlay tracks the image as it is
    -- rescaled.
}

invariant FocusRegionIsNotRecroppable {
    -- The focus region records what was actually targeted. It is
    -- sometimes tighter or looser than a person would draw by hand,
    -- and that is accepted. Letting it be redrawn would make the
    -- evidence a matter of opinion, and the machinery to overlay a
    -- correction costs more than the imprecision does.
    --
    -- Someone who thinks the region misleads says so in a
    -- TraceAnnotation. This is settled, not deferred.
}

invariant DialogueValuePrivacy {
    -- The dialogue text written into a captured step NEVER contains
    -- the verbatim value typed into a text_input, password_input or
    -- text_area. The verb describes the act ("Escribir en email"),
    -- not the content. For password_input, no aspect of the typed
    -- value (length, characters, shape) is encoded — only the act.
    --
    -- Selection-committed events (dropdown, checkbox, radio) DO
    -- include the chosen option text, because that text is choice
    -- metadata, not free user input.
}

invariant UserLayerSeededOnlyOnStrongSignals {
    -- The user layer is what the person experienced, and the recorder
    -- cannot see that. It seeds the layer anyway, but only where the
    -- page states the outcome plainly enough that a wrong guess is
    -- unlikely:
    --
    --   - landing on a confirmation / success screen immediately after
    --     a submit seeds config.icon_user_success ("pix-happy" in the
    --     author's shorthand).
    --
    -- Everything else leaves the cell empty. An error is deliberately
    -- NOT a signal: a person meeting a validation message may be
    -- annoyed, indifferent or relieved, and the recorder has no
    -- standing to say which.
    --
    -- The bar is high on purpose. An empty cell asks to be filled in;
    -- a wrongly-seeded one has to be noticed first, and a plausible
    -- wrong seed is worse than no seed at all.
}

invariant RecorderSeedsVisibleLayersOnly {
    -- At capture time the recorder writes cells only for the layers
    -- score.visible_layers names. Under layout = pix the environment
    -- and supporting_processes cells are seeded empty.
    --
    -- It never blanks a cell that already carries content. Layout
    -- governs visibility alone, never storage — see core's
    -- LayersAreHiddenNeverDiscarded. A score switched sb -> pix keeps
    -- what was in its hidden rows, and recording against it must not
    -- be the thing that quietly clears them.
}

invariant SingleActiveScore {
    recorder.state = recording implies exists recorder.active_score
    recorder.state = paused    implies exists recorder.active_score
    recorder.state = idle      implies recorder.active_score = null
}

invariant SingleLiveSession {
    -- The recorder holds at most one open session, and holds one
    -- exactly when it is engaged. Two live sessions would interleave
    -- snapshots from different sittings into one movement, which is
    -- exactly what the session boundary exists to prevent.
    recorder.state = recording implies exists recorder.active_session
    recorder.state = paused    implies exists recorder.active_session
    recorder.state = idle      implies recorder.active_session = null
}

invariant SessionAppendsRatherThanReplaces {
    -- A trace has exactly one trace per score and grows across
    -- sittings. Each RecordingSession appends one Movement and appends
    -- its snapshots; none of them touches what an earlier session
    -- wrote.
    --
    -- The earlier stance in this spec was that re-recording was
    -- forbidden. It is not: a person who records the same task twice
    -- is comparing two runs, and throwing the first away is the one
    -- outcome that makes the second recording pointless.
    for a in RecordingSessions:
        for b in RecordingSessions:
            a != b and a.trace = b.trace implies a.movement != b.movement
}

invariant StepPositionsAreContiguous {
    for m in Movements:
        for st in m.steps:
            st.position >= 0 and st.position < m.steps.count
}

invariant TraceCardinality {
    -- Score and ScreenshotTrace are 1:1, for the life of the score.
    -- Re-recording does not create a second trace; it appends to this
    -- one.
    for t in ScreenshotTraces:
        t.score.trace = t
}

invariant TraceSnapshotMatchesScoreStep {
    for s in TraceSnapshots:
        s.step.movement.score = s.trace.score
}

invariant SnapshotBelongsToItsSessionsMovement {
    -- A snapshot lands in the movement its session opened. This is
    -- what keeps a second sitting from writing into the first
    -- sitting's movement.
    for s in TraceSnapshots:
        s.step.movement = s.session.movement
}

invariant CaptureDerivedFieldsImmutable {
    -- Once a TraceSnapshot has been written, no rule modifies any of
    -- its fields. The whole snapshot can be deleted (UserDeletesStep
    -- cascade, UserDeletesTrace, UserDeletesScore) — append-only is
    -- per-field, not per-entity.
    --
    -- Commentary about a snapshot lives in TraceAnnotation, which is
    -- mutable and separate. The recorder never creates one: an
    -- annotation is a person's reading of the evidence, added in the
    -- viewer, and the recorder has nothing to say.
}

invariant RecordingSurvivesNavigationAndTabs {
    -- Top-level navigations in the tab being recorded — including
    -- cross-origin hops, redirects through 3DS flows, and the
    -- eventual return to the original origin — do not change
    -- Recorder.state.
    --
    -- Recording also follows the user across tabs. When a click on
    -- a recorded page opens a new tab (target=_blank, window.open,
    -- middle-click, ctrl-click, "open in new tab" from context
    -- menu), the recorder begins capturing in that new tab against
    -- the same active session. The first captured snapshot in the new
    -- tab carries boundary = crossing iff the host differs from the
    -- previous snapshot's host (see BoundaryReflectsHostChange) and
    -- captured_tab_id reflects the new tab.
    --
    -- The number of host crossings and tab switches within a single
    -- movement is unbounded.
}

invariant MultiTabStaysLinear {
    -- Tabs annotate; they do not branch. captured_tab_id marks each
    -- snapshot, a tab switch opens a section divider, and the
    -- partitura stays one linear sequence of steps.
    --
    -- This matters more now than it used to. A Movement means a
    -- recording session — one sitting at the recorder. Giving a tab
    -- its own movement would overload the construct with a second,
    -- incompatible meaning, and a trace with four movements would no
    -- longer tell you whether you were looking at four sittings or
    -- four tabs.
    --
    -- Parallel flows are a viewing problem, and the viewer solves it
    -- with the tab annotation.
}

invariant TabIdentityRecorded {
    -- Every TraceSnapshot the recorder writes records the browser tab
    -- where the capture occurred. The walkthrough viewer uses this to
    -- annotate consecutive snapshots that came from different tabs,
    -- per @guarantee TabIdentityVisibleInViewer in
    -- walkthrough-viewer.allium.
    for s in TraceSnapshots:
        s.captured_tab_id != ""
}

invariant BoundaryReflectsHostChange {
    -- A snapshot's boundary is `crossing` exactly when its
    -- captured_from_url is on a different host than the previous
    -- snapshot's captured_from_url in the same trace.
    for t in ScreenshotTraces:
        for s in t.snapshots:
            let prev = preceding_snapshot(t, s)
            (s.boundary = crossing)
                = (exists prev
                   and host_of(prev.captured_from_url) != host_of(s.captured_from_url))
}

invariant SectionStartsOnScreenChange {
    -- A captured ScoreStep has step_title != "" exactly when, vs the
    -- previous captured step in the same movement:
    --   - it is the first step in the movement, OR
    --   - the captured_from_url changed, OR
    --   - the captured_page_title changed, OR
    --   - the captured_tab_id changed (user switched tab and
    --     captured something in the other tab), OR
    --   - SpaScreenChangeStartsSection left a pending section title
    --     (an in-place screen change with none of the above).
    -- Otherwise step_title is empty.
    --
    -- This invariant constrains only the seed value at capture time.
    -- The user can edit step_title freely after capture.
    for m in Movements:
        for st in m.steps:
            let snap = st.snapshot
            let prev_step = preceding_step(m, st)
            let prev_snap = preceding_snapshot_of_step(m, st)
            exists snap implies
                (st.step_title != "")
                    = (not exists prev_step
                       or not exists prev_snap
                       or prev_snap.captured_from_url != snap.captured_from_url
                       or prev_snap.captured_page_title != snap.captured_page_title
                       or prev_snap.captured_tab_id != snap.captured_tab_id
                       or had_pending_section_title(st))
}

invariant SpaSectionsAreEnumerated {
    -- In-place screen changes are named as an explicit series beneath
    -- the last real section name, which is the document title or the
    -- screen's name as SectionStartsOnScreenChange observed it:
    --
    --     Carro                 <- real screen change, ordinal reset to 0
    --     Carro: Paso 1         <- in-place change
    --     Carro: Paso 2         <- in-place change
    --     Pago                  <- real screen change, ordinal reset to 0
    --
    -- The base name is inherited, never invented; the recorder only
    -- enumerates beneath it, using config.spa_section_step_label. Where
    -- there is no base yet — an in-place change before any real screen
    -- change — no section is started at all, because a bare "Paso 1"
    -- names nothing.
    --
    -- The numbering is a placeholder that puts the divider in the right
    -- column. Renaming it is expected, and is what the editor is for.
}

invariant ScoreStateTransitionExplicit {
    -- A Score's state changes only via UserMarksScoreAsFinal or
    -- UserReopensScoreAsDraft. No rule mutates state automatically.
    -- In particular, stopping a recording does not promote it: a
    -- recording stays draft until someone says otherwise.
}

invariant StoragePressureIsAdvisory {
    -- The library is bounded by weight, not by count. Twenty
    -- recordings full of screenshots and twenty typed partituras are
    -- wildly different loads on the profile's quota, and only one of
    -- them threatens it.
    --
    -- On crossing config.library_pressure_fraction of the profile's
    -- quota — or config.score_count_backstop scores, where the browser
    -- reports no quota at all — the user is warned and offered a
    -- backup export. Nothing else happens. No save is refused, no
    -- score is evicted, and recording is never blocked because the
    -- library is full.
    --
    -- Refusing or evicting would destroy captured evidence that exists
    -- nowhere else, on a judgement the software is not in a position
    -- to make. The policy itself belongs to core; this spec's part is
    -- to never gate capture on it.
}

invariant IdsAreMintedNotReused {
    -- Score, Movement, ScoreStep, RecordingSession and TraceSnapshot
    -- ids are minted fresh and never reused. The uniqueness statements
    -- live with the entities, in score-contract.allium
    -- (StableIdsAreUnique, MovementIdsAreUnique, StepIdsAreUnique).
    --
    -- What matters here is that the recorder mints and never rewrites:
    -- a step id is the join to its snapshot, so reassigning one
    -- silently reattaches evidence to the wrong moment.
}

-- ============================================================
-- Actor Declarations
-- ============================================================

-- The external party at this boundary is code, not a person: the
-- browser's extension runtime, delivering DOM events into the recorder
-- and rendering its state back out.
actor BrowserExtensionRuntime {
    identified_by: Recorder where state in { idle, recording, paused }
}

-- ============================================================
-- Surfaces
-- ============================================================

surface BrowserHost {
    facing browser: BrowserExtensionRuntime

    exposes:
        browser.state
        browser.active_score
        browser.active_session
        browser.pending_section_title

    provides:
        UserCreatesScore(layout: ScoreLayout, title: String?)
        UserStartsRecording(score: Score)
        UserPausesRecording(session: RecordingSession)
        UserResumesRecording(session: RecordingSession)
        UserStopsRecording(session: RecordingSession)
        UserAddsBlankStep(movement: Movement)
        UserEditsCell(step: ScoreStep, layer: ScoreLayer, new_value: Cell)
        UserEditsScoreMetadata(score: Score, title: String?, description: String?, layout: ScoreLayout?)
        UserMarksScoreAsFinal(score: Score)
        UserReopensScoreAsDraft(score: Score)
        UserDeletesStep(step: ScoreStep)
        UserDeletesScore(score: Score)
        UserDeletesTrace(score: Score)

        -- Capture event sources (from content scripts):
        UserClicksElement(element: InteractiveElement)
        UserBlursTextInput(element: InteractiveElement, text_changed: Boolean)
        UserChangesSelection(element: InteractiveElement, new_value: String)
        UserAttachesFile(element: InteractiveElement, file_count: Integer, file_names: List<String>)
        UserDragsAndDrops(source: InteractiveElement, target: InteractiveElement)
        MediaElementEvent(media: MediaElement, event_kind: MediaEventKind)
        ErrorBecameVisible(indicator: ErrorIndicator)
        HoverRevealedContent(element: InteractiveElement, revealed_text: String, duration: Duration)
        SignificantDomMutation(page: WebPage, changed_fraction: Decimal)

        UserExportsScoreAsPiXJson(score: Score)
        UserExportsScoreAsPdf(score: Score)
        UserImportsPiXScore(target_score: Score, document: PiXScoreDocument)

    @guarantee NoNetworkSideEffects
        -- No rule sends data to a remote service. Recordings live
        -- entirely inside browser-local storage.

    @guarantee LocalOnlyPersistence
        -- Scores and screenshot traces persist in browser-local
        -- storage. The canonical home is the editor's IndexedDB.
        -- Scores are not synced across devices and not exposed to
        -- other extensions.

    @guarantee RecordingStateAlwaysVisible
        -- Whenever Recorder.state in {recording, paused}, the user
        -- sees a persistent visual indicator that the recorder is
        -- engaged. Recording and paused are visually distinct (e.g.
        -- pulsing red dot vs steady amber dot). The indicator is
        -- visible on every tab where the recorder might capture.
        -- It disappears only after UserStopsRecording.

    @guarantee ReRecordingIsAnnounced
        -- Starting a recording against a score that already has a
        -- trace tells the user, before capture begins, that this is a
        -- second sitting appended to the first, and how many sittings
        -- the score already carries. Nothing is overwritten, and the
        -- surface says so — a person about to re-record is entitled to
        -- expect the opposite, because most recorders do overwrite.

    @guarantee CrossSiteCaptureScope
        -- The boundary marker on a TraceSnapshot is metadata only:
        -- it describes that the user crossed hosts since the
        -- previous snapshot. It does not enable broader capture on
        -- the new host. Pages that block content-script injection
        -- (browser-internal pages, certain bank-side iframes) cannot
        -- be captured; recording on them is silent (no step, no
        -- placeholder).

    @guarantee RecordingPersistedOnStop
        -- On UserStopsRecording, the active Score and its
        -- ScreenshotTrace are persisted to the editor's canonical
        -- library. If the editor is unreachable at that moment
        -- (offline, dev server down, prod URL not configured),
        -- the data remains in extension storage as a pending sync
        -- until a successful flush. The recording is never
        -- silently dropped.

    @guarantee StoragePressureWarnsAndOffersBackup
        -- On crossing config.library_pressure_fraction the surface
        -- tells the user how full the library is and offers to export
        -- a backup before anything is deleted. It never refuses a
        -- save, never evicts, and never refuses to start a recording.
        -- The choice of what goes is the user's, made with the
        -- evidence in front of them.
        --
        -- Where the browser reports no quota, the count backstop
        -- applies and the warning says so, rather than implying a
        -- measurement that was never taken.

    @guarantee PrivacyOfTypedValues
        -- Per invariant DialogueValuePrivacy: typed text from
        -- text_input, password_input, text_area and contenteditable
        -- never appears in any captured cell. The user can later
        -- enrich the dialogue text in the editor — that's a
        -- post-capture authoring decision, not a capture decision.

    @guarantee ImportRejectionExplained
        -- When UserImportsPiXScore(target, document) is rejected
        -- because target.id != document.score_id, the surface
        -- explains the mismatch and offers a re-export of target
        -- as the recovery path. The extension never silently
        -- creates a new Score from a foreign document.
}

-- ============================================================
-- Open Questions
-- ============================================================

open question "Hover-reveal capture: HoverRevealCriteria detects tooltips/popovers via DOM mutation during dwell. Some sites render content on hover via CSS-only (no DOM change) — those reveals are invisible to the recorder. A heuristic (computed-style change on a specific element) is possible but expensive to run on every dwell. Still deferred."

open question "Provenance has no home in the contract. The recorder writes ScoreProvenance (user agent, extension version, timezone, locale) once at Score creation, and this spec's external view of Score carries the field. score-contract.allium's Score does not. Either core takes provenance — it is capture-derived, so it arguably belongs beside the trace rather than on the score — or this spec stops writing it. Until that is settled the two documents disagree about what a Score carries."

open question "Naming the base of an SPA section series. SpaScreenChangeStartsSection inherits last_section_base from the last real screen change and enumerates beneath it. Where the recording opens directly onto an SPA — no real screen change has happened yet — there is no base, and the rule declines to start a section at all, so in-place changes before the first navigation are invisible. Is falling back to the document title at session start good enough, or should the recorder ask the user to name the screen once at the start of a sitting?"

open question "Detecting the high-confidence success signal. UserLayerSeededOnlyOnStrongSignals commits to seeding config.icon_user_success when a submit lands on a confirmation screen, but does not say how the recorder recognises one. Candidate signals: a navigation immediately after a text_committed or click on a submit control, plus a page whose text matches confirmation tokens; or the absence of any ErrorIndicator within a window after submit. The second is cheaper and locale-agnostic but weaker. Needs a criteria invariant of the same kind as ErrorDetectionCriteria before it can be implemented."
